From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32, explorer: the folder view as an automation object (3687)

shell32, explorer: the folder view as an automation object

The IShellFolderViewDual3 of a folder view (what scripts reach as the
Document of an Explorer window, and what IShellView::GetItemObject
returns for SVGIO_BACKGROUND and IDispatch) now answers Folder,
SelectedItems, FocusedItem, SelectItem (by FolderItem or position),
SelectItemRelative, CurrentViewMode, FolderFlags, IconSize, ViewOptions,
GroupBy and SortColumns. shelldispatch.c exports the constructors the view
needs to hand out Folder, FolderItem and FolderItems objects for its
folder and selection. The shell browser window of the desktop returns its
folder view as its Document.
---
